course: dictionary
lesson: 11558
title: A collection of wise sayings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a kind of writing. When you meet a new one, look at the words around it for clues. «Our teacher read us short sayings from the Analects of Confucius.» The clues are short sayings and Confucius, who is a teacher, so analects must be sayings or writing chosen from a wise teacher.
explain: Notice the capital letters. «The Analects» with capitals is the name of one famous book. Written with a small letter, «analects» means any collection of short sayings chosen from a writer or teacher. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Each week we copy one of the analects into our books.» Each week, and copying into books, tells you that analects are short pieces of writing you can copy and think about. You do not need to know every word to follow the sentence; the clues do the work.
fact: Analects means a collection of short sayings or pieces of writing chosen from a writer or teacher.
fact: The Analects is the famous book of sayings of Confucius, a wise teacher in ancient China.
fact: The Analects has a capital A and a capital T because it is the name of one special book.
fact: The Analects of Confucius teach kindness, respect for parents, good manners and learning.
fact: Context clues, such as the words sayings and teacher, help you work out what analects means.
exercise: «Our teacher read us short sayings from the Analects of Confucius.» What is the Analects? | A type of fast car | A map of ancient China | *A famous book of short sayings by a wise teacher | A kind of school bag
exercise: Priya says analects are long stories about dragons. What are analects really? | Long stories about dragons | *Short sayings or pieces of writing chosen from a writer or teacher | Songs sung at birthday parties | Maths problems to solve
exercise: «Each week we copy one of the analects into our books.» Which word in the sentence names these short sayings? | *analects | week | each | books
test: «The Analects of Confucius teach kindness, respect and good manners.» What do The Analects teach? | *Kindness, respect and good manners | How to build a boat | Fast running | How to cook rice
test: Which word means a collection of short sayings chosen from a teacher? | Anagram | Anatomy | *Analects | Analysis
exam: «In religious education we read the analects of a wise teacher from ancient China.» What are the analects in this sentence? | A kind of ancient coin | Stories about animals | A list of school rules | *Short sayings or writings chosen from a wise teacher
